        "original_id": "43d828ca-577a-56b8-a5a0-32d7ea5ae08f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Hoch Conservatory\n- People: Clara Schumann, Johannes Brahms, Bernhard Cossmann\n- Places: Frankfurt\n- Roles: faculty, teacher of cello\n\nFacts:\n- In 1878, Bernhard Cossmann helped found the Hoch Conservatory in Frankfurt.\n- In 1878, Bernhard Cossmann became teacher of cello at the Hoch Conservatory.\n- In the late 19th century, Clara Schumann served on the faculty of the Hoch Conservatory.\n- In the late 19th century, the Hoch Conservatory achieved international renown with distinguished teachers such as Clara Schumann.\n- Clara Schumann was the first person to perform publicly any work by Johannes Brahms.",
